From 31038795214802284006850e689cc7f78dcaf513 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:25:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/34] drm/gma500: add sgxfive GPU address spaces

Add the sgxfive VM context ioctls: CREATE/DESTROY_VM_CONTEXT give each client
address space its own SGX page directory, and VM_MAP/VM_UNMAP place exact,
non-overlapping, page-aligned ranges of a BO (read-only on request) inside
the user heaps of the REV1 layout, never in the reserved firmware heaps. A
mapping pins its BO's pages, and the next firmware command invalidates the
BIF caches. Per-file state comes from new open/postclose hooks, which also
tear down a closing client's VMs. KUnit checks the range rules.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
